# Task 4 Independent Review

## Verdict

**FAIL — 1 Critical, 3 Important, 0 Minor findings.**

The implementation gets the schema, canonical serializer, inert-default checks, constructor/checkpoint
ordering, and future publication wiring mostly right. It does not yet provide a truthful immutable digest
of the behavior that can actually execute.

## Findings

### Critical — The policy digest can silently diverge from runtime behavior

**Confidence: 10/10.**

`PortfolioSimulator` builds and hashes the policy once at construction
(`core/backtest_engine.py:1424-1427`), then later execution continues to read mutable policy inputs:

- signal cadence reads `self.signal_every_n_days` at `core/backtest_engine.py:1677`;
- position sizing reads `self.position_risk_pct` and `self.stop_loss_pct` at
  `core/backtest_engine.py:2501-2510`;
- stagnation and EMA exits read simulator attributes at `core/backtest_engine.py:2619-2634`;
- CANSLIM scoring reads live `settings.CANSLIM_WEIGHT_*` globals in
  `backtest.py:340-359`; and
- scale-out execution reads live `settings.SCALE_OUT_TIERS` at
  `core/backtest_engine.py:2604-2614`, while the policy merely snapshots that global at
  `core/engine_policy.py:415-419`.

None of those public simulator attributes or module settings is frozen, and the existing suite even
uses post-construction mutation of `max_positions`/`enable_eviction`
(`tests/test_backtest_engine.py:534-535`, `561-562`, `586-587`, `613`, `727`). `_result_config`
publishes the stored object and stored digest without rebuilding from live state
(`core/backtest_engine.py:2023-2024`). The PIT check likewise recomputes the hash of the stored snapshot,
not of current effective inputs (`pit_baseline.py:1474-1482`).

Consequently, a caller or later optimizer can change actual sizing, exits, cadence, capacity, gates, or
global weights/tiers after construction and still receive the original policy SHA. The checkpoint
fingerprint then binds the stale SHA (`core/backtest_engine.py:1239`), so the core attestation and resume
guarantee can be false while all digest checks pass.

Required fix: make execution consume an immutable captured policy state, or rebuild and compare a complete
live policy before fingerprinting, execution, result creation, and publication. Hashing the already stored
dict again is not sufficient.

### Important — Active cadence, industry filtering, and M policy are outside the classified/digested surface

**Confidence: 9/10.**

The schema omits material active behavior despite the requirement that behavior-bearing fields be
truthful, classified, sourced, and digest-bound:

- `signal_every_n_days` changes which sessions can produce signals
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:1677-1690`). It is present only as an unclassified raw result-config value
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:1997`) and a legacy checkpoint-fingerprint field
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:1225`); it is absent from `_SimulatorPolicy` and every policy helper
  (`core/engine_policy.py:36-57`, `474-490`).
- Normal provider-mode runs load an industry map (`core/backtest_engine.py:1588-1589`) and reject symbols
  outside the ranked groups (`core/backtest_engine.py:2280-2287`). The active top-N and minimum-group-size
  policies come from `config/settings.py:59-60` and are applied at
  `core/industry_group.py:16-49`. Only top-N is copied to raw result config
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:2022`); minimum size, whether the filter is active, its source/classification,
  and both values in the effective-policy digest are missing.
- `_market_policy_fields` records only the two constructor booleans
  (`core/engine_policy.py:292-309`), but the M score and bullish result used by the engine come from
  `evaluate_m` (`core/backtest_engine.py:698-705`), whose weights, bullish threshold, and rising lookback
  are live settings (`core/canslim/m_market_direction.py:354-368`). Those active M policies are neither in
  the effective policy nor truthfully exposed elsewhere in result config.

The cadence raw field is truthful as far as its value goes, and its separate legacy fingerprint does
protect resume from cadence changes. That still does not satisfy the required leaf wrapper or make cadence
part of the canonical policy digest. Industry minimum-size/filter-mode and M evaluator settings have no
equivalent protection. Runs with materially different entry selection can therefore share the same
effective-policy SHA.

Required fix: inventory all active engine behavior, at minimum cadence, industry-filter activation/top-N/
minimum-size, and M evaluation settings, and add classified/source-bearing leaves whose values are the ones
execution actually consumes.

### Important — The new `min_c_a_growth` check breaks supported injected strategies and can misstate their scoring policy

**Confidence: 10/10.**

For any injected strategy, the constructor converts a missing `min_c_a_growth` attribute to `None`
(`core/backtest_engine.py:1330-1334`). The compatibility validator accepts only a finite numeric default
(`core/engine_policy.py:108-125`), so a custom strategy that never requested this inert
`CanslimStrategy` field now fails before construction completes. This is not rejection of a non-default
inert request; it is rejection because an unrelated custom strategy has no such request surface.

That path is supported intentionally: `PortfolioSimulator` tracks injected strategies and binds their
canonical engine-owned fields (`core/backtest_engine.py:1376-1407`), and the custom-strategy contract uses
an object with only `evaluate_market`/`evaluate_symbol`
(`tests/test_backtest_custom_strategy_contract.py:69-81`, instantiated at `120-125`). The change therefore
adds a behavior regression beyond the task's allowed fail-closed rejection of explicit non-default inert
arguments. Policy construction also unconditionally dereferences the same attribute
(`core/engine_policy.py:465-469`).

Even an injected strategy that happens to define the attribute is described as if it used the built-in
metric selection and CANSLIM scoring: `_scoring_policy_fields` discards `simulator` and always emits the
built-in settings (`core/engine_policy.py:232-289`), while the injected execution path obtains the row from
`self.strategy.evaluate_symbol` (`core/backtest_engine.py:2307-2315`) and only re-applies the engine-owned
entry contract afterward (`core/backtest_engine.py:2139-2229`).

Required fix: apply the `min_c_a_growth` inert check only to the built-in `CanslimStrategy` policy surface
(or otherwise preserve absent-field compatibility), and represent injected-strategy mode/identity so the
policy does not claim built-in scoring behavior that did not produce the signal.

### Important — The early-winner leaf does not describe the exits that actually remain active

**Confidence: 10/10.**

The policy says a `+20%` winner within 15 days gets a `hold_through_trading_day: 40`
(`core/engine_policy.py:405-413`). Actual execution clears `eight_week_hold` at the start of day 40
(`core/backtest_engine.py:2586-2598`), before that day's exit processing. More importantly, the flag does
not create a general hold: the hard stop is always checked (`2600-2602`), and stagnation, protective-stop,
and EMA exits remain active (`2619-2634`). Only tiered scale-outs are guarded by
`not trade.eight_week_hold` (`2604-2618`).

Thus the leaf overstates both the day-40 boundary and the scope of the hold. Because Task 4 must expose
current behavior without changing strategy semantics, the policy should say precisely that the trigger
suspends scale-out tiers while the flag is active, that the flag is cleared when `days_held >= 40`, and
that the other listed exits remain active.

## Verified task requirements

- `PolicyClassification` has the four exact values, `_field` requires the enum, and canonical JSON rejects
  NaN/non-JSON-safe values (`core/engine_policy.py:23-29`, `60-93`).
- The requested entry thresholds, component weights, C/A settings, non-M composite, institutional
  reweighting, market/regime booleans, capacity values, risk inputs, configured exit thresholds, and scale
  tiers are present and correctly classified at snapshot time (`core/engine_policy.py:170-420`).
- The risk target is algebraically `portfolio_equity * position_risk_pct / stop_loss_pct`
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:2501-2510`); `position_size_pct` is reported unsupported, not effective
  (`core/engine_policy.py:447-452`).
- Inert validation rejects booleans, `None`, NaN/infinity, and non-default finite values with the required
  absolute tolerance and source-bearing error (`core/engine_policy.py:96-125`). It is invoked before
  `DataFetcher` construction (`core/backtest_engine.py:1322-1346`, `1375`).
- Canonical digesting uses sorted compact UTF-8 JSON with `allow_nan=False`
  (`core/engine_policy.py:60-66`, `494-497`). The digest exists by the end of construction
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:1424-1427`) before the run creates a checkpoint fingerprint
  (`core/backtest_engine.py:1483-1496`).
- Result config contains the policy and digest (`core/backtest_engine.py:2023-2024`). On the only successful
  manifest-publication path, `effective_policy` and `effective_policy_digest` are defined and verified
  before summary writes (`pit_baseline.py:1474-1503`) and remain in scope for top-level manifest creation
  (`pit_baseline.py:1524-1557`). `canslim_config` also retains both through `active_config`.
- `core/engine_policy.py` does not import `core.backtest_engine`; the inspected import path does not create a
  circular import. The exact Task 4 package changes only the three authorized production files and does not
  rewrite a sealed Task 11 artifact.

## Review constraints observed

No tests, backtest, provider/network command, cache refresh, optimizer operation, or Git mutation was run.
Production sources were inspected read-only; only this review artifact was written.
